The Chinese State Council presented its Next-Generation Artificial Intelligence Development Plan in July 2017.
The Chinese National Natural Sciences Foundation provides funding to people in academic institutions in a similar way to that used by the National Science Foundation and other government organizations to fund researchers in the United States. However, the quality of academic work is lower in China, Lee said.
Earlier this year, the U.S. Department of Defense instituted a Joint Artificial Intelligence Center, which is intended to involve industry and academic partners, and the White House announced the formation of the Restricted Committee for Artificial Intelligence.
