Palin faces charges for three Class A offences, meaning he could be sentenced to a sentence of up to one year and fined 250,000 dollars.
He was also charged for a class B offense, punishable by a day in jail and a fine of 2,000 dollars.
This is not the first time criminal charges have been filed against Palin.
In December 2017 he was accused of assaulting his father, Todd Palin.
The mother, Sarah Palin, called the police to report the alleged attack.
The case is being tried by the Alaska Veterans Court.
In January 2016 he was charged with domestic violence, interference in reporting a crime of domestic violence and possession of a gun under the influence of alcohol, in relation to the incident.
His girlfriend accused him of punching her in the face.
Sarah Palin was criticized in 2016 by veterans' associations after associating her son's violent behavior with post-traumatic stress stemming from her service in Iraq.
