The airline responsible for the plane that crashed into a lagune in Micronesia, Pacific, now reports that there is a man missing after having communicated that all 47 passengers and crew had been safely rescued from the sinking plane.
In a statement, Air Niugini stated that since Saturday afternoon, it was unable to confirm the whereabouts of a male passenger.
The area company said it was collaborating with hospitals, investigators and local authorities to locate the man.
