Bill Jaynes, an American passenger, claimed that the plane was coming very low.
"It's the best that's happened," Jaynes said.
Jaynes said that he and other people had managed to drag themselves with the water by the waist and get to the plane's emergency exits sinking.
He recounted that the flight attendants had panicked and started screaming, and that he had suffered a minor head injury.
According to the U.S. Navy, the sailors who were working on a wet-enhancing work nearby also helped the rescue by resorting to an inflatable boat to transport people to land before the plane sank 30 meters (100 feet) deep.
