When he announced that he was not going to enter a formal campaign, the emotions came from above - gratitude for the people who had supported her, frustration with a system that raises so many obstacles to fundraising and getting the message to the voters, rather than the delegates, and anger against sexism - and the tears arose.
"It even seemed depressed," Patricia Schroeder recalled when speaking of the media reaction.
"I would have thought Kleenex was my business sponsor.
What would you write in my epitaph now?
“Did she weep?”
